new-page: true
on-arrival: media_event_done = 1; news_headline = "The Left discovers how little media it owns"

= January 2020 — A campaign without an ecosystem

Public television speaks for PiS; commercial news reduces politics to PiS
against KO. We can still place good guests, but we have no daily operation to
turn a report from Wałbrzych or Elbląg into tomorrow's national argument.

- @media_newsroom
- @media_subscription
- @media_personalities
- @media_wait

@media_newsroom
title: Fund a campaign newsroom and rapid-response team
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Slow-looking, durable capacity.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; media_strategy = "Professional network"; media_relationship = "Owned newsroom and trained guest network"; media_capacity += 12; local_network += 3; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "A small newsroom begins to contest the first frame"

We hire researchers and producers, train our guests and give regional contacts
somewhere to send a story. There is no grand launch. The candidate simply
stops discovering the day's hostile question on air.

- @nik_removal_2020: Turn to the removal attempt

@media_subscription
title: Build the operation around subscriptions and a membership drive
subtitle: +1 resource and modest reach. Organisers spend the month asking the same supporters twice.
on-arrival: resources += 1; media_strategy = "Supporter subscription"; media_relationship = "Supporter-funded mailing and video operation"; media_capacity += 4; local_network += 2; organiser_energy -= 4; young_support += 1; barons_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Subscriptions finance a small Left media operation"

Our appeal produces recurring donors and a mailing list we control. It does
not produce enough reporters to answer every hostile broadcast.

- @nik_removal_2020: Turn to the removal attempt

@media_personalities
title: Put everything behind recognisable personalities
subtitle: Immediate reach; the organisation remains hollow.
on-arrival: media_strategy = "Leader-led campaign"; media_relationship = "Leader access without owned distribution"; media_capacity += 5; left_poll += 0.4; spring_strength += 2; barons_dissent += 3; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The candidate becomes the entire media strategy"

Bookings increase, but every success now belongs to the candidate—and so does
every mistake. Our local candidates wait for material that never arrives.

- @nik_removal_2020: Turn to the removal attempt

@media_wait
title: Save the money for the formal campaign
subtitle: Resources survive; hostile frames compound.
on-arrival: media_strategy = "Reactive"; media_relationship = "Reactive bookings and borrowed audiences"; media_capacity -= 2; left_poll -= 0.3; public_trust -= 2; news_headline = "The Left again answers yesterday's story"

We preserve the treasury and leave the press office answering yesterday's
story. By the formal campaign, our opponents have already chosen the frame.

- @nik_removal_2020: Turn to the removal attempt

@nik_removal_2020
# prose-audit: Grade B — The removal attempt reads back the November decision in prose and in what the player may still choose, and the audit-referral option is visibly locked to the earlier defence; the chamber's own auditors remain offstage.
title: The auditor they cannot remove
subtitle: PiS tries to end Banaś's term and finds the law it wrote
face-image: img/poland/events/marian-banas-2019.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.nik_removal_2020_done = 1;
Q.nik_removal_pressure = 1;
Q.pis_poll_momentum = (Number(Q.pis_poll_momentum) || 0) - 0.15;
Q.institutional_issue_salience =
    (Number(Q.institutional_issue_salience) || 0) + 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The governing majority fails to remove the head of the audit chamber";
!}

= January 2020 — The term holds

Prosecutors move on the property file. The Sejm majority looks for a route to
end the term early and finds none that survives contact with the statute it
passed itself: dismissal requires grounds the government cannot manufacture in
a fortnight, and the immunity it granted is now working exactly as written.

Banaś stays. Within weeks the <span class="tooltip-text" style="color:#666" title="Najwyższa Izba Kontroli (NIK) — the Supreme Audit Office, a Sejm-answerable constitutional auditor whose president holds a fixed six-year term.">Supreme Audit Office</span> begins publishing findings
on government programmes with a bluntness nobody has seen from it in years — a
watchdog with nothing left to lose and a personal reason to bite.

[? if nik_stance = "Institutional defence": In November we defended the office
rather than the man, and the chamber's staff noticed which caucus did that.?]
[? if nik_stance = "Resignation demanded": In November we demanded his head.
The chamber's staff noticed that too, and the referral desk is not returning
our calls.?]
[? if nik_stance = "Campaign centrepiece": Our presidential campaign has been
running on state capture since November, and this month supplies the
evidence.?]
[? if nik_stance = "Stayed out": We had no position in November, which means we
have no relationship with the institution now and no story about it either.?]

- @nik20_hold_term
- @nik20_strip
- @nik20_refer_audits
- @nik20_watch

@nik20_hold_term
title: Vote against every route to an early dismissal
subtitle: Keeps the six-year term intact and makes the chamber's later findings harder for PiS to dismiss as revenge.
on-arrival: {!
Q.nik_removal_response = "Term defended";
Q.nik_independence = (Number(Q.nik_independence) || 50) + 15;
Q.nik_government_hostility =
    (Number(Q.nik_government_hostility) || 20) + 10;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 5;
Q.constitutional_restraint =
    (Number(Q.constitutional_restraint) || 0) + 4;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 4;
Q.news_headline =
    "The audit chamber's term survives on opposition votes";
!}

The removal routes fail, several of them on our votes. The government has
learned that an office it designed to be safe from everybody else is also safe
from it.

For the rest of this parliament the Supreme Audit Office is an institution the
cabinet cannot control and cannot quiet. Every programme it examines from here
lands as a finding rather than as a party complaint.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@nik20_strip
title: Support stripping his immunity and let the prosecutors decide
subtitle: Consistent with a November resignation demand; it also lets a government use prosecution to reach an auditor.
on-arrival: {!
Q.nik_removal_response = "Immunity stripped";
Q.nik_independence = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.nik_independence) || 50) - 10
);
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.institutional_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) - 4
);
Q.prosecution_independence = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.prosecution_independence) || 0) - 3
);
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica votes to send the audit chief to the prosecutors";
!}

The immunity goes and the file moves to a prosecution service that answers, in
the end, to the justice minister. Nobody in the chamber pretends this is only
about a tenement.

The audit office survives with a president who now spends his time on his own
defence. Its findings, when they come, will be received as the work of a man
under charges — which is precisely the outcome the majority wanted and could
not achieve by dismissal.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@nik20_refer_audits
title: Send the chamber our own list of programmes to audit
subtitle: Requires having defended the office in November. Converts a hostile watchdog into a permanent opposition research capacity.
choose-if: nik_stance = "Institutional defence" or nik_stance = "Campaign centrepiece"
unavailable-subtitle: The chamber does not take referrals from the caucus that demanded its president resign — or from one that had no position at all.
on-arrival: {!
Q.nik_removal_response = "Referral channel opened";
Q.nik_referral_channel = 1;
Q.nik_independence = (Number(Q.nik_independence) || 50) + 10;
Q.nik_government_hostility =
    (Number(Q.nik_government_hostility) || 20) + 12;
Q.institutional_trust = (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) + 4;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 3;
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "The audit chamber begins taking referrals from the Left's caucus";
!}

Because we defended the office rather than the officeholder, a door is open
that is closed to everybody else. Our deputies begin sending the chamber
subjects: emergency procurement, public-media financing, foundation grants,
state-company contracts.

An opposition without ministries has just acquired an investigative body with
statutory access to documents. It is not ours, it will not be told what to
find, and it is now the single most useful institution in the country to a
party with no executive power at all.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@nik20_watch
title: Stay out of the removal fight
subtitle: Leaves the outcome to the governing camp and keeps our hands clean of both sides.
on-arrival: {!
Q.nik_removal_response = "Abstained";
Q.nik_independence = (Number(Q.nik_independence) || 50) + 3;
Q.nik_government_hostility =
    (Number(Q.nik_government_hostility) || 20) + 6;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) - 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The removal attempt collapses without the opposition's involvement";
!}

The attempt fails on the majority's own divisions. We are not part of the
story, which is comfortable and forgettable in equal measure.

The chamber becomes hostile to the government anyway. It simply owes nothing
to anyone, which means its findings will arrive when it chooses and be handed
to whoever is standing nearest.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue
